<%= l_ui_title_bar(
  title: "Search",
  breadcrumbs: [
    ["Home", root_path]
  ]
) %>

<p class="mt-4">Styled search form components for filtering and querying content.</p>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Basic usage</h2>

<form action="/search" method="get" class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <div class="l-ui-search-inline">
    <div class="l-ui-search-control l-ui-search-control--clearable">
      <label for="query" class="l-ui-sr-only">Search</label>
      <input type="text" id="query" name="query" class="l-ui-form__field" placeholder="Search...">
      <button type="button" class="l-ui-search-control__clear" aria-label="Clear search">
        <svg class="l-ui-icon--xs" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 6 18 18M18 6 6 18" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--primary">Search</button>
  </div>
</form>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-search-basic-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-search-basic-heading">Basic search</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;form action="/search" method="get" class="l-ui-form"&gt;
  &lt;div class="l-ui-search-inline"&gt;
    &lt;div class="l-ui-search-control l-ui-search-control--clearable"&gt;
      &lt;label for="query" class="l-ui-sr-only"&gt;Search&lt;/label&gt;
      &lt;input type="text" id="query" name="query"
             class="l-ui-form__field" placeholder="Search..."&gt;
      &lt;button type="button" class="l-ui-search-control__clear"
              aria-label="Clear search"&gt;...&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;button type="submit" class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--primary"&gt;Search&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">CSS classes</h2>

<div class="l-ui-table-container mt-4">
  <table class="l-ui-table">
    <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Search CSS classes</caption>
    <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Class</th>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-search-inline</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Inline layout for a search input and button side by side</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-search-control</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Wraps the field and its clear button, giving them a positioning context of their own</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-search-control--clearable</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Leaves room in the field so a long term scrolls under the button rather than behind it</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-search-control__clear</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">The clear button inside the field's trailing edge. 24x24, the smallest target WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 accepts</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-form__field</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Text input styling</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-button--primary</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Submit button</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-button--outline</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Clear/reset button</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l-ui-sr-only</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Visually hidden label for accessibility</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">With the ransack gem (optional)</h2>

<p class="mt-4">See the <%= link_to "Ransack integration", ransack_path %> page for a live example and installation instructions.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Use the <code>l_ui_search_form</code> helper to render a styled search form. In simple mode, pass <code>fields:</code> to generate a single search input that searches across multiple columns:</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface mt-4"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_search_form(@q, url: users_path, fields: [:name, :email]) %&gt;</code></pre>

<p class="mt-4">This generates a combined <code>name_or_email_cont</code> predicate - a single input that matches any of the listed fields.</p>

<h3 class="mt-8">Searching as you type</h3>

<p class="mt-4">Pass <code>live: true</code>, with a <code>turbo_frame:</code> for the response to land in, and there is no Search button to press: the form submits as the field changes, debounced so a typed word is one request rather than one per letter. The field carries its own clear button, which appears only once there is something to clear, and Escape in the field clears it too.</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface mt-4"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_search_form(@q, url: users_path, fields: [:name, :email],
                     turbo_frame: "users", live: true, count: @pagy.count,
                     page_param: "users_page") %&gt;</code></pre>

<p class="mt-4">It is opt-in, and a frame alone does not turn it on: where a response renders and whether typing should submit at all are separate decisions. <code>live: true</code> without a <code>turbo_frame:</code> raises, since a keystroke would otherwise mean a full page load.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Each search <em>replaces</em> the history entry rather than pushing one, so Back leaves the collection instead of replaying the term letter by letter. The URL still carries the term, so a search stays shareable and survives a reload. The action is set on the form, which Turbo reads before the frame's own, so sort links and pagination inside the same frame still advance.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Two details matter for accessibility, and both need something from you:</p>

<ul class="l-ui-list mt-4">
  <li>Pass <code>count:</code>. With no button to press, a screen reader is told nothing when results change - the count is announced through the layout's live region, which sits outside every frame so it is not replaced by the render it is describing.</li>
  <li>The caret is preserved across the frame render that answers a search, so a typed word is never interrupted mid-letter. This is handled for you.</li>
</ul>

<p class="mt-4">The <%= link_to "Ransack integration", ransack_path %> page runs both modes side by side: the Users collection passes <code>live: true</code> and searches as you type, the Posts collection leaves it alone and submits only when asked to.</p>

<p class="mt-4">A form left non-live keeps a visible Search button, and still clears from inside the field: clearing means clearing the field and submitting, which the Stimulus controller does, and that goes on any form given a <code>turbo_frame:</code>. Escape in the field clears it too.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Only a form with no <code>turbo_frame:</code> has no controller, and so no clear button. To put a clear beside one, build the link yourself and give it <code>data-action="click-&gt;l-ui--search-form#clear"</code>, which rewrites the href so another collection's params survive the navigation. Asking for <code>clear:</code> without a frame raises.</p>

<p class="mt-4"><code>count:</code> and <code>min_chars:</code> describe typing, so they mean nothing to a form that submits when asked to: passing one to a form that is not live raises rather than being quietly dropped.</p>

<h3 class="mt-4">Options</h3>

<div class="l-ui-table-container mt-4">
  <table class="l-ui-table">
    <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Helper options</caption>
    <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Option</th>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Default</th>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>fields</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>[]</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Attribute names to search. Combined with OR into a single input. Required in simple mode.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>predicate</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>:cont</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Ransack predicate (<code>:cont</code>, <code>:eq</code>, <code>:start</code>, etc.)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>combinator</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>:or</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">How fields are combined (<code>:or</code> matches any field, <code>:and</code> requires all)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>label</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>"Search"</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Label text for the input</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>placeholder</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Auto-generated</td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Placeholder text. Defaults to "Search by name, email, ..."</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>button</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>nil</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Text for a <em>visible</em> submit button. In live mode, left unset, the submit is present but neither seen nor tabbed to - it is what Enter and a browser with no JavaScript submit through. A non-live form always gets a visible button, since it needs one that can be pressed.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>clear</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>true</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">The clear button built into the field, on by default whenever <code>turbo_frame:</code> is given. Pass <code>false</code> to omit it, or a string to name it. Clearing means clearing the field and submitting, which the Stimulus controller does, so asking for it without a frame raises.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>live</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>false</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Search as the user types. Opt-in, and requires <code>turbo_frame:</code> - without one it raises, since a keystroke would mean a full page load. Left alone, the form submits only when asked to.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>count</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>nil</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">The size of the result set, announced to screen readers after each search. Live mode only. Without it nothing is announced, and <code>live: true</code> with no count logs a warning in development.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>min_chars</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>0</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Hold the search back until the term is this long. Live mode only</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>page_param</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>"page"</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Pagy's page key for this collection, dropped when carrying other collections' params across a submit. Pagy's <code>page_key:</code> is yours to choose and bears no fixed relation to the Ransack <code>search_key</code>, so it is passed rather than guessed.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>url</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>nil</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Form action URL</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>html</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><code>{}</code></td>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Additional HTML attributes for the form tag</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3 class="mt-4">Custom usage</h3>

<p class="mt-4">Pass a block for full control over the form layout. The partials <code>search_field</code> and <code>search_select</code> apply l-ui styling to individual fields:</p>

<div class="mt-4" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-search-custom-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-search-custom-heading">Custom search form</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_search_form(@q, url: users_path) do |f| %&gt;
  &lt;%= render "layered_ui/shared/search_field",
              form: f, field: :name_cont, label: "Name" %&gt;

  &lt;%= render "layered_ui/shared/search_select",
              form: f, field: :role_eq, label: "Role",
              options: %w[admin editor viewer] %&gt;

  &lt;div class="l-ui-form__group l-ui-form__group--large-gap"&gt;
    &lt;%= f.submit "Search", class: "l-ui-button l-ui-button--primary" %&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>
